# VectorMind - public deployment configuration
#
# Copy this file to deployment/.env and fill in the values.
# deployment/.env is gitignored - the DOMAIN and TLS_EMAIL values are
# committed nowhere.
#
# Required by the TLS overlay (deployment/docker-compose.tls.yml) and by
# deployment/deploy.ps1. DOMAIN needs an A record resolving to this
# machine's public IP BEFORE Caddy starts (the Let's Encrypt HTTP-01
# challenge is answered on port 80, so issuance fails while DNS is still
# propagating).

# The public hostname the demo will be served under. Free option:
# duckdns.org (an A record in real DNS, so Caddy/Let's Encrypt work with
# it). Otherwise any domain whose DNS you control.
DOMAIN=demo.duckdns.org

# An address Let's Encrypt can mail certificate-expiry notices to.
TLS_EMAIL=you@example.com

# Optional. The app's own port, published on loopback only when the TLS
# overlay is active (127.0.0.1:FRONTEND_PORT). 8080 is reserved for it.
# FRONTEND_PORT=8080